{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.CommRing","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.Supported","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.Variables","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Finsupp.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FinCases","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator"],"declarations":37,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.exists_not_interiorMarkov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.exists_not_interiorMarkov","kind":"theorem","line":462,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L462-L464","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.exists_not_interiorMarkovFar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.exists_not_interiorMarkovFar","kind":"theorem","line":456,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L456-L460","doc":"Existence form, for citation: some Markov tower violates the interior rule\neven in its commuting form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.not_interiorMarkov_cmTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.not_interiorMarkov_cmTower","kind":"theorem","line":452,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L452-L454","doc":"**(S1) is not a consequence of the tower axioms.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.not_interiorMarkovFar_cmTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.not_interiorMarkovFar_cmTower","kind":"theorem","line":439,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L439-L450","doc":"**The commuting form of (S1) is not a consequence of the tower axioms.**\nIn `cmTower`, with `g = 0`, `a = 1` and `b = σ_2² ∈ ⟨σ_2, …⟩`,\n`tr (a * σ_0 * b) = 0` but `z * tr (a * b) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmTr_X2_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmTr_X2_sq","kind":"theorem","line":434,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L434-L437","doc":"The other side: `tr (X₂²) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmTr_X0_X2_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmTr_X0_X2_sq","kind":"theorem","line":422,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L422-L431","doc":"The value the interior rule would need: `tr (X₀ * X₂²) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmTower_σ_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmTower_σ_zero","kind":"theorem","line":416,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L416-L419","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmTower_σ_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmTower_σ_two","kind":"theorem","line":411,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L411-L414","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmTower","kind":"def","line":386,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L386-L407","doc":"The counter-model tower: `σ_i = X_i` for `i < 3`, `σ_n = 1` above, `z = 1`,\n`H n` = polynomials in the variables of index `< n`, trace `cmTr 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmTr_mul_X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmTr_mul_X","kind":"theorem","line":371,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L371-L383","doc":"Markov at a genuine variable: for `a` supported below `n`,\n`cmTr (a * X n) = z * cmTr a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmF_add_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmF_add_single","kind":"theorem","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L343-L369","doc":"The single-monomial Markov step: for `n < 3` and `μ` with zero exponents at\nindices `≥ n`, `cmF (μ + e_n) = z * cmF μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.exponent_eq_zero_of_mem_supported","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.exponent_eq_zero_of_mem_supported","kind":"theorem","line":332,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L332-L341","doc":"A monomial in the support of a polynomial supported on `{i | i < n}` has\nzero exponent at every index `≥ n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmTr_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmTr_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L326-L330","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmTr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmTr","kind":"def","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L322-L324","doc":"The trace of the counter-model: the linear extension of `cmF`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.cmF","kind":"def","line":315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L315-L320","doc":"The monomial functional: `z^{|μ|}` on squarefree monomials, `1` on `X₂²`,\n`0` otherwise.  Only `z = 1` is used below, but the Markov check goes through for\nevery `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.interiorMarkov_ascending","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.interiorMarkov_ascending","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L292-L301","doc":"**(S1) holds for ascending `b`.**  For `a ∈ H g` and `b = σ_{g+1} ⋯ σ_{g+k}`,\n`tr (a * σ_g * b) = z * tr (a * b)`, from the Markov axioms alone.  This is the\nmonotone case, and it is the whole of what the axioms give. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.tr_mul_asc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.tr_mul_asc","kind":"theorem","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L278-L290","doc":"Iterated stabilisation: `tr (a * asc n k) = z ^ k * tr a` for `a ∈ H n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.asc_mem_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.asc_mem_upper","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L273-L276","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.asc_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.asc_mem","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L266-L271","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.asc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.asc","kind":"def","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L261-L264","doc":"The ascending word `σ_n * σ_{n+1} * ⋯ * σ_{n+k-1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.tr_bondWord_of_interiorMarkov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.tr_bondWord_of_interiorMarkov","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L224-L257","doc":"**(S3) — the `A`-bond product**, conditional on `InteriorMarkov`.\n\nFor a chain `x * (σ_{g₀}+d₀) * y₀ * (σ_{g₁}+d₁) * y₁ * ⋯ * y_{A}` with strictly\nincreasing bonds, blocks between them, and `x` below the first bond,\n\n  `tr (bondWord) = (∏_k (z + d_k)) * tr (freeWord)`.\n\nInduction on the number of bonds; each step is (S2) at the leading bond with\n`a := x` and `b :=` the entire remainder of the chain, then the remainder is\nre-associated so that the next block joins the prefix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.bondWord_mem_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.bondWord_mem_upper","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L204-L222","doc":"Everything from a chain's first block onward lies above every bond `g` at or\nbelow the chain's head bond. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.bondWord_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.bondWord_mul","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L196-L202","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.freeWord_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.freeWord_mul","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L188-L194","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.bondWord_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.bondWord_cons","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L183-L185","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.freeWord_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.freeWord_cons","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L180-L181","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.headBond","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.headBond","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L173-L177","doc":"The bond generator at the head of a chain (`0` for the empty chain, in which\ncase the hypothesis mentioning it is vacuous). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.ChainOK","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.ChainOK","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L164-L171","doc":"The chain hypotheses: bonds strictly increase along the chain, each block\nlies above the bond preceding it, and each block that is followed by a bond lies\nbelow that bond. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.freeWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.freeWord","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L159-L162","doc":"The same chain with every bond letter deleted: `x * y₀ * y₁ * ⋯`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.bondWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.bondWord","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L153-L157","doc":"`x * (σ_{g₀} + d₀) * y₀ * (σ_{g₁} + d₁) * y₁ * ⋯`, associated as\n`x * ℓ₀ * (y₀ * ℓ₁ * (y₁ * ⋯))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.tr_bond_of_interiorMarkov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.tr_bond_of_interiorMarkov","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L137-L145","doc":"**(S2)** `tr (a * (σ_g + d • 1) * b) = (z + d) * tr (a * b)`, for `a` below\nand `b` above the bond, **conditional on `InteriorMarkov`**.  Linearity only. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.InteriorMarkov.far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.InteriorMarkov.far","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L132-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.InteriorMarkovFar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.InteriorMarkovFar","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L126-L130","doc":"The weaker \"commuting\" form: `b` generated by `σ_{g+2}, …` only, so that\n`b` commutes with `σ_g` by far-commutation.  Implied by `InteriorMarkov`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.InteriorMarkov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.InteriorMarkov","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L116-L124","doc":"**(S1) — the interior-Markov statement**, as a `Prop` about a tower.\n\nFor every bond `g`, every `a` below it and every `b` above it,\n`tr (a * σ_g * b) = z * tr (a * b)`.  This is the statement the route-C probe\nmeasured on the canonical non-monotone nucleon word.  It is *not* a field of\n`MarkovTower`: `exists_not_interiorMarkov` below shows it is independent of the\ntower axioms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.upper_anti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.upper_anti","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L107-L114","doc":"`upper` is antitone: a word above a higher bond is above every lower bond. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.σ_mem_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.σ_mem_upper","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L102-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovInteriorBond.upper","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovInteriorBond.lean#L96-L100","doc":"The subalgebra generated by the generators **strictly above** the bond `g`:\n`σ_{g+1}, σ_{g+2}, …`.  A word for the nucleon block above the bond lives here;\nit need not be monotone and need not commute with `σ_g`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}